    "# Supervised Learning and Linear Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "## Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "**Supervised learning** is a machine learning approach where a model learns from a dataset containing known **inputs** and corresponding **outputs**.\n",
    "\n",
    "A typical workflow is:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Training Data\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "Learning Algorithm\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "Model f\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "New Input x\n",
    "     ↓\n",
    "Prediction ŷ\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Training Set\n",
    "\n",
    "A **training set** contains examples used to train the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each training example consists of:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Input feature (`x`)** — information used to make a prediction.\n",
    "* **Target (`y`)** — the known output associated with the input.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example\n",
    "\n",
    "| Input Feature | Target      |\n",
    "| ------------- | ----------- |\n",
    "| House size    | House price |\n",
    "| 120 m²        | $300,000    |\n",
    "| 180 m²        | $450,000    |\n",
    "| 250 m²        | $600,000    |\n",
    "\n",
    "The model learns the relationship between house size and house price from these examples.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Model and Predictions\n",
    "\n",
    "The learning algorithm produces a **model**, represented by a function `f`.\n",
    "\n",
    "The model takes an input `x` and produces a prediction:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{y} = f(x)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Symbol | Meaning                |\n",
    "| ------ | ---------------------- |\n",
    "| `x`    | Input feature          |\n",
    "| `y`    | Actual target value    |\n",
    "| `ŷ`    | Predicted target value |\n",
    "| `f`    | Learned model          |\n",
    "\n",
    "The prediction `ŷ` is an estimate of the true target `y`.\n",
    "\n",
    "After training, the model can be used to make predictions for new inputs.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Linear Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "**Linear regression** is a supervised learning algorithm used to predict **continuous numerical values**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples include:\n",
    "\n",
    "* House prices\n",
    "* Temperature\n",
    "* Vehicle range\n",
    "* Energy consumption\n",
    "* Sales revenue\n",
    "\n",
    "When there is only **one input feature**, the model is called **univariate linear regression**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The model is represented by:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "f_{w,b}(x) = wx + b\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "or equivalently:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{y} = wx + b\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "* `x` — input feature\n",
    "* `w` — parameter controlling the slope\n",
    "* `b` — parameter controlling the intercept\n",
    "* `ŷ` — predicted value\n",
    "\n",
    "The model therefore represents a straight line through the data.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Training a Linear Regression Model\n",
    "\n",
    "The training data can be visualized as points on a graph:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Price\n",
    "  ^\n",
    "  |                         •\n",
    "  |                    •\n",
    "  |                •\n",
    "  |           •\n",
    "  |       •\n",
    "  |   •\n",
    "  +------------------------------> House Size\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The learning algorithm determines values for `w` and `b` that define the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "Once trained, the resulting line can be used to predict the price of a house based on its size.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Regression vs. Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "Supervised learning problems can be divided into different types.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Regression predicts a **continuous numerical value**.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Input: 200 m² house\n",
    "Output: $480,000\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "Classification predicts a **discrete category**.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Input: Image\n",
    "Output: Dog\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "| Problem        | Output                     |\n",
    "| -------------- | -------------------------- |\n",
    "| Regression     | Continuous numerical value |\n",
    "| Classification | Discrete category          |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Training Example Notation\n",
    "\n",
    "Individual training examples are indexed using a superscript:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x^{(i)}, y^{(i)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where `i` identifies the training example.\n",
    "\n",
    "If there are `m` training examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "i = 1, 2, ..., m\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For example:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x^{(1)}, y^{(1)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "represents the first training example.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notation:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x^{(47)}, y^{(47)}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "represents the 47th training example.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Note:** The superscript indicates the example index; it is not an exponent.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Concepts\n",
    "\n",
    "| Concept                      | Description                              |\n",
    "| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n",
    "| Supervised Learning          | Learning from input-output examples      |\n",
    "| Training Set                 | Dataset used to train the model          |\n",
    "| Feature (`x`)                | Input used for prediction                |\n",
    "| Target (`y`)                 | Known desired output                     |\n",
    "| Prediction (`ŷ`)             | Model's estimated output                 |\n",
    "| Model (`f`)                  | Function learned from training data      |\n",
    "| Regression                   | Predicts continuous numerical values     |\n",
    "| Classification               | Predicts discrete categories             |\n",
    "| Linear Regression            | Regression using a linear model          |\n",
    "| Univariate Linear Regression | Linear regression with one input feature |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Core Formula\n",
    "\n",
    "For univariate linear regression:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{f_{w,b}(x) = wx + b}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This simple equation provides a foundation for understanding how machine learning models learn relationships between inputs and outputs.\n"
   ]
